/**
 * The L8 contract (second round), held from the console's side.
 *
 * Every response below was captured from the backend's own app at commit
 * 6ee0368 (a snapshot of backend/ and runtime/, so nothing was read from a
 * tree being edited), driven in-process through its doors with a TestClient:
 * the scratchpad capture reuses backend/tests/l8b.py and the
 * test_l8_canary.py, test_l8_templates.py, test_l8_deliverables.py and
 * test_l8_capture_gaps.py fixtures without editing them. Ada (administrator)
 * authors and configures, Rui (operator with the policy-reviewer group)
 * reviews, Tia (operator with the template-certifier group) certifies, Oli
 * (operator) reads. A canary taking half the queued starts, read with its
 * arms, refused for a candidate nobody measured and again once its own
 * production runs drifted from the benchmark, ended; one replaced, whose
 * candidate's retry went back to production when it ended; a shadow on the
 * queue whose pairs were pending, compared, disagreeing and skipped on a
 * stand-in, ended with its queued shadow job withdrawn; a shadow in process
 * journalling would-call while production waited at the report gate in the
 * inbox with its deliverable, approved and published, a second refused and
 * withdrawn; the budget with a shadow's spend beside it; a worker's
 * deliverables moved forward only, a file gone, one outside the outbox, one
 * changed on disk, an SDK's claims; templates made, refused, certified and
 * cut, with lineage and drift; the runs list's marks, the queue's jobs, the
 * eval sets through the backend, the paused 409, the retirement's id, and
 * the spine of an agent deployed before L8 and after a rollback. Inlined as
 * captured, except that the capture's temporary workspace is written
 * `/workspace` in every path. Each test calls the real client (lib/api/l8b.ts,
 * and l8.ts, l5.ts, the generated client lib/api/l2.ts reads through) with
 * fetch stubbed, then the helpers and components the pages render with, and
 * checks that what the page shows comes through. When a door changes,
 * capture it again and replace the fixture.
 */

